sequenceDiagram
    participant S as LiDAR
    participant P as Perception
    participant M as 2.5D map
    participant G as Geometry hazards
    participant C as Cost map and planner
    participant V as Vehicle
    S->>P: sweep at 10 Hz
    P->>M: classified points into height-range cells
    M->>G: ray-cast, expected vs observed returns
    G->>C: hazard cells (NEGATIVE_OBSTACLE, UNKNOWN)
    P->>C: PEDESTRIAN / VEHICLE tracks
    C->>V: A* path around hazards
    C->>V: safe speed = f(detection range, braking)
    Note over G,C: Conservatism Invariant - losing information never lowers cost
